r_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct end-to-end SMTP, mailbox, rejection-policy, preservation, and platform evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is strong for both nodes: pre-restart identity and health, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data/connectivity were captured and independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots. Operational hygiene is high, with only two apparently retained precautionary backup files as minor residue.","limitations":["Native package-health checks timed out in all lifecycle phases, so package-manager consistency was not independently established.","No final /etc inventory directly confirms the two backup files still exist; their retention is inferred from their successful creation and the absence of a later removal command in the complete timeline."]}
